# text=auto eol=lf normalizes future commits to LF; nothing here changes
# today (repo is already all-LF outside tests/golden).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Frozen fixture bytes. golden_replay.py's check_pack() sha256-hashes the
# pack files here (photo-profile.json, owner .md) via Pack.snapshot(), so any
# line-ending conversion breaks the pin — that is the real bug this guards:
# a Windows clone with the default core.autocrlf=true converted those LF pack
# files to CRLF on checkout and reported drift on 4 of 8 dumps while every
# data row still matched. The CSVs' CRLF is separate and legitimate:
# csv.DictWriter's default \r\n terminator, written with newline="". -text
# means git never converts either direction, on any platform, regardless of
# what core.autocrlf is set to locally.
tests/golden/** -text
